Chapter: PunctualMatchRecursion

 A punctual function whose self-recursion hides inside a match arm,
 and one whose self-recursion hides inside a let binding value.
 CDX6005 must reject recursion regardless of which expression form
 carries it; an earlier checker walked only the match scrutinee and
 the let body, so both of these compiled clean with a WCET report
 that understated the true cost unboundedly.

Section: Definitions

  punctual spin : Integer -> Integer
  spin (n) =
   when n
    is 0 -> 0
    is otherwise -> spin (n - 1)

  punctual spin-let : Integer -> Integer
  spin-let (n) =
   if n == 0 then 0
   else let deeper = spin-let (n - 1)
   in deeper

  opening : Integer = 0
